<lesson id="les-l7-02-city-services" title="City services on the ring" level="7" minutes="18" goal="The hospital reaches the city services and the public district cannot reach the cameras"/>
<step n="1" text="Two services hang on the ring: the hospital in DistrictEast and the traffic cameras in DistrictWest. Ping CityCamera from SouthResident. It answers today, and it should not."/>
<step n="2" text="On DistrictWest make access list 170: deny 192.168.73.0 to 192.168.74.0 (wildcard 0.0.0.255), then permit everything else."/>
<step n="3" text="Apply list 170 outbound on GigabitEthernet0/0, the port the cameras hang on." check="c1"/>
<step n="4" text="Ping CityServices from CityHospital. The hospital must keep its line to the city." check="c2"/>
<check id="c1" kind="noreach" from="pc0" to="cam0" url="" expect="" label="The public district cannot reach the cameras"/>
<check id="c2" kind="ping" from="pc1" to="server0" url="" expect="ok" label="The hospital reaches CityServices"/>
<check id="c3" kind="ping" from="pc0" to="server0" url="" expect="ok" label="The public district still reaches CityServices"/>
